%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:dumb-receiver -- DumbTcp acknowledges each data segment at once, also with the delayed ACK on.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of DumbTcp (its NED comment): a very simple algorithm that sends an
ACK for each segment.

The class dumb-receiver: DumbTcp::receiveSeqChanged() sends an ACK at once. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test
separates "dumb" from the other algorithms, which delay the ACK (delayedAcksEnabled, the
default).

Host under test: host1, with DumbTcp, which listens at the port 1000; host2 connects and sends
10000 bytes (7 segments) at 0.2 s. Observation: level 1, host1 sends at least 7 ACKs of data
until the ACK of all data.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: dumb-receiver
%# value: "DumbTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassDumbTcpReceiver")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host2")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo > {isn2} + 1 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("acks")
                                        .describe("each ACK of data of host1")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 1 + 10000")
             .assertPacket("{acks} >= 7")
             .describe("the ACK of all data")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassDumbTcpReceiver compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DumbTcp"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpEchoApp"
*.host1.app[0].localPort = 1000
*.host1.app[0].echoFactor = 0
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host2.app[0].connectAddress = "host1"
*.host2.app[0].connectPort = 1000
*.host2.app[0].tOpen = 0.1s
*.host2.app[0].tSend = 0.2s
*.host2.app[0].sendBytes = 10000B
*.host2.app[0].tClose = 1000s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassDumbTcpReceiver: PASS
